===========================================================================
VERDICT: PASS -- both MAC authentication and Web authentication
===========================================================================

PART A -- MAC AUTHENTICATION                                        PASS
  baseline (auth-mac off):  known MAC 10/10, unknown MAC 10/10
  with `auth-mac enable` on port2.0.2:
      UNKNOWN MAC 0000.dead.beef  ->  0/10   BLOCKED
      KNOWN   MAC 00f0.4d00.7717  ->  9/10   AUTHORISED
  show auth supplicant:
      authorizedSupplicantNum: 1
      macBasedAuthenticationSupplicantNum: 1
      Supplicant name: 00-f0-4d-00-77-17
      Supplicant address: 00f0.4d00.7717
      authenticationMethod: MAC-based Authentication

  *** THE USERNAME FORMAT MATTERS AND IS NOT OBVIOUS ***
  The DUT sends the MAC to RADIUS as **00-f0-4d-00-77-17** -- lowercase hex,
  HYPHEN separated. A RADIUS user named `00f04d007717` (the common
  no-separator form) does NOT match and the supplicant fails with fail:T.
  There is no `auth-mac username-format` command on this build to change it
  ("% Unrecognized command"), so the RADIUS user must be created in the
  hyphenated form. This cost the first run of this case a false FAIL.

  Second gotcha: default host-mode is single-host, so one FAILED supplicant
  occupies the port and a subsequent good MAC never gets to authenticate.
  `auth host-mode multi-supplicant` is what let both be tested on one port.

